id: pm-csv-join-plans
title: Resolve cross-table external references before CSV import
description: "Plan joins across explicitly selected external tables. Existing CSV relational columns accept native IDs and table-schema.ts negotiates one table; provider adapters retain remote-key ownership. Core continues to own item identities, relationships and transactions."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T22:22:43.054Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T04:45:16.249Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "A three-table fixture resolves all unique references in one preview; ambiguous keys produce zero mutations; apply uses reviewed source digests and SDK transaction primitives. Every mutation path uses shared explicit relationship/scope intent; random focus and cwd changes cannot add unreviewed relationships, and divergent old scope refuses replay. Public join APIs expose only JoinRefusal and preserve lower-level source codes and remedies for malformed CSV, encoding and SDK failures."
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T22:22:45.644Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: inspected core SDK contracts, CSV relational import/export and single-table schema contracts, plus Jira, Linear, ADO and Beads adapters. No cross-selected-table external-key join planner found. Provider key mapping remains adapter-owned; join declarations are explicit. Validation will cover non-git trackers, stale revisions, ambiguous/unresolved coordinates, replay, and SDK state readback. Host write-fencing limitation is already tracked by pm-csv-sdk-write-fence."
  "2026-10-25T22:24:03.715Z",codex-agent,"Implement bounded create-only cross-table plans. SDK-generated native IDs are persisted in reviewed plans; external keys never become native identities. Plans embed captured CSV sources with exact SHA-256 digests, explicit scalar mappings and parent/blocked_by declarations. Validate the whole selected graph before writes. Use the SDK create lifecycle and workspace transaction coordinator; inspect exact owned history and current documents on every retry, skip foreign collisions and their dependents, and refuse edited owned targets. No additional shared cache/outbox/lease files. Append-only compensation closes only unchanged owned creates, never deletes tracker records."
  "2026-10-25T22:36:34.558Z",codex,"Targeted tests pass for three-table resolution, zero-byte preview/refusals, foreign-target skip closure, stale owned revisions, strict boundary fuzz, SDK journal transitions, compact commands and safe reconciliation. Model testing uses separate real SDK trackers as the reference oracle so normalization is never hand-written. The pinned SDK normalizes custom status IDs; tests now consume its returned ID. It accepts completedAt only for its configured close status, a host capability limitation to report."
  "2026-10-25T22:39:08.419Z",codex-agent,"Public main tracker validation: 127 items across 3 selected tables; 19 native parent targets resolved as explicit key joins; 40833 CSV bytes; 114-byte receipt; 46173-byte plan; injected duplicate reported both coordinates. Read-only source hashes unchanged, zero tracker writes, no git executable. Final recovery contract retains created rows rather than closing them during compensation. Committed SDK journals bypass step inspect, so apply additionally rereads all current target revisions after coordination."
  "2026-10-25T22:46:34.543Z",codex-agent,"Seeded model validation passed: 500 sequences, 4000 operations, 16 randomized custom-status tracker/model pairs. Every supported scalar, parent and dependency is compared by reading native SDK state from both trackers; older plan replay, source changes, LF/CRLF and whitespace are included. Behavioral revert proof: disabling only compile external-key edge resolution makes the three-table regression fail on the SDK-read parent value. Local strict health otherwise passes but reports the pre-existing global pm-github host-version skew tracked by pm-csv-sdyz; no dependency pin or global installation was changed."
  "2026-10-25T22:49:39.689Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and local verification are complete: 13 focused regressions plus the 500-sequence model test; real CLI JSON/TOON in a tracker with no Git; strict input/output fuzz; current-revision checks after committed-journal fast paths; zero duplicates found; docstrings documented. npm typecheck and lint were run through pm test --run --progress. Full npm/Bun release checks will run in CI and their final run URL/counts will be attached to the PR. Isolated-global strict health passes; normal host health only reports the already tracked pm-github skew."
  "2026-10-25T22:51:13.499Z",codex-agent,"Final artifact explicitly binds expected target revision \"absent\" in the transaction identity; retries still verify exact owned create history through the SDK. Receipts cap coordinate details at 20 while retaining complete counts and remedies. Repeated public-copy measurement after this final artifact field: 127 rows, 3 tables, 19 references, 40833 CSV bytes, 114-byte receipt, 46193-byte plan, 2 duplicate coordinates, zero writes, unchanged source hash. Focused checks still pass."
  "2026-10-26T04:18:51.612Z",codex-agent,"Review follow-up: close the ambient-default class across all package mutation paths using one explicit relationship/scope builder, including SDK focus suppression through unset parent. Wrap lower-level join CSV and IO refusals into JoinRefusal with source code/remedy context. Add randomized ambient-state SDK-readback properties and malformed-input regressions, behavioral revert proofs, and fresh exact-head CI gates. Existing implementation and previous gate evidence are retained."
  "2026-10-26T04:33:32.764Z",codex-agent,"Mutation audit: SDK creates in joins and lineage now share buildMutationIntent; legacy create/update and marker cleanup render scope arguments from that builder. Raw SDK patches/restores wrap the same builder inside the existing item-lock callback, preserving unselected current scope. Empty selected scope is explicitly unset; absent create links are explicitly cleared. SDK appends an explicit_unset audit suffix to create messages, so ownership matching retains the caller marker while preserving SDK audit evidence. Join and legacy atomic replay now recheck reviewed scope before trusting cached receipts; lineage rejects old inherited scope as identity conflict."
  "2026-10-26T04:39:55.893Z",codex-agent,"Ambient property model passed 500 seeds and 4000 reviewed-state operations over 16 non-git target/reference tracker pairs. Target focus is randomized before preview, between preview/apply and during replay; two different working directories per pair are selected repeatedly. Scope cells vary empty and explicit values; expected native values are read from separate SDK trackers. Focus/assignment/planning changes produce no extra parent/dependency links. Malformed quote, ragged-row, mixed/bare newline and invalid UTF-8/JSON boundary tests pass with JoinRefusal and retained sourceCode/remedy. Legacy update compensation remains governed by native SDK revision checks, with the new legacy scope guard limited to create receipt reuse."
  "2026-10-26T04:43:23.223Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: reverting only the builder parent-unset branch makes the focused focus-change test fail (an inherited parent is detected after native create); restoring it passes. Reverting only previewJoins refusal wrapping makes the malformed-CSV test fail its JoinRefusal instance assertion; restoring it passes. Targeted coverage across join-plans.ts and mutation-intent.ts is 100% lines, branches and functions. The 500-sequence ambient model passed; focused native compensation/recovery reruns passed after limiting cached-scope checks to create receipts."
  "2026-10-26T04:45:14.853Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up checks passed: linked pm test run executed all 6 mutation-intent regressions; native step-applied crash, compensation crash and concurrent-writer compensation checks passed; 500 ambient-state sequences passed. Focused join/builder coverage is 100% in all dimensions. Documentation now states explicit create clears, legacy keyed-import empty scope clears, preserve-current patch/restore intent, sourceCode/remedy wrapping and rejection of old inherited scope. Full npm/Bun release gates will be rerun in CI on the pushed follow-up head."
